    "error": "openrouter moonshotai/kimi-k3: overloaded (no tool_call despite forced tool_choice) -- {\"id\":\"gen-1788863229-U1603YVC4kbV0Y60fkul\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1788863229,\"model\":\"moonshotai/kimi-k3\",\"provider\":\"Sail Research\",\"system_fingerprint\":null,\"service_tier\":null,\"choices\":[{\"index\":0,\"logprobs\":null,\"finish_reason\":\"length\",\"native_finish_reason\":\"length\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":null,\"refusal\":null,\"reasoning\":\"Let me analyze each pair carefully.\\n\\n**Requirement 0**: \\\"What is the id of the semester that had both Masters and Bachelors students enrolled?\\\"\\n\\nQuery:\\n```sql\\nSELECT DISTINCT T2.semester_id FROM Degree_Programs AS T1 JOIN Student_Enrolment AS T2 ON T1.degree_program_id = T2.degree_program_id \\nINTERSECT \\nSELECT DISTINCT T2.semester_id FROM Degree_Programs AS T1 JOIN Student_Enrolment AS T2 ON T1.degree_program_id = T2.degree_program_id WHERE degree_summary_name = 'Bachelor'\\n```\\n\\nThe first part of the INTERSECT has no WHERE clause — it should filter for 'Master'. The query name says \\\"drop_where_conjunct\\\" — the WHERE degree_summary_name = 'Master' was dropped. So the first set is ALL semesters with any enrollment, and the second is semesters with Bachelor enrollments. The intersection is just semesters with Bachelor enrollments (since Bachelor semesters ⊆ all semesters). This does NOT capture \\\"both Masters and Bachelors\\\".\\n\\nThe back-translation says: \\\"The set of semester IDs associated with any degree program and student enrollment is identical to the set of semester IDs associated with degree programs named 'Bachelor'...\\\" Hmm, the back-translation's English is a bit odd — it says the sets are \\\"identical\\\", and the postcondition says \\\"The result is empty if these sets are identical.\\\" Wait, that's wrong — INTERSECT returns the intersection, which would be empty only if the sets are disjoint. Actually the back-translation's postcondition says \\\"Returns the intersection of two queries: (1) all distinct semester IDs from enrollments in any degree program, and (2) all distinct semester IDs from e"
  },
